    {
      "association_text": "Enterobacteriaceae relative abundance was elevated approximately 10-fold in critically ill ICU patients compared to healthy controls during the first week of ICU admission, as measured by 16S rRNA sequencing of rectal swabs in a prospective cohort of 51 patients, representing the dominant compositional shift in ICU-associated gut dysbiosis.",
