    },
    {
      "association_text": "Progressive Enterobacteriaceae enrichment (≥2-fold increase between consecutive ICU time points) was independently associated with significantly increased odds of nosocomial infection (OR 6.8, 95% CI 1.7–25.3, p=0.01) compared to ICU patients without progressive enrichment, in a prospective cohort of 51 critically ill adults.",
